findings:
- finding_id: I1
  title: Dependencies inline instead of workspace level
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Dev added chrono and uuid to Cargo.toml but no mention of workspace-level
    dependencies. Reviewer did not flag inline dependency versions.
- finding_id: I2
  title: 'FieldErrorCode missing #[non_exhaustive]'
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged [MEDIUM]: ResponseEnvelope and ErrorDetail are not #[non_exhaustive]\
    \ \u2014 but this was about response structs, not FieldErrorCode specifically.\
    \ FieldErrorCode itself was not mentioned."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Hardcoded trace_id 'none'
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: TEA wrote tests expecting trace_id in meta, but no test asserts trace_id
    derives from request context rather than being hardcoded. Reviewer did not flag
    hardcoded 'none' trace_id.
- finding_id: I4
  title: Zero structured logging
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged [MEDIUM]: 'Zero structured logging / tracing instrumentation\
    \ \u2014 No #[instrument] on handlers. No tracing::info!(), tracing::warn!(),\
    \ or tracing::error!() calls.'"
- finding_id: I5
  title: Security comment claims tracing that doesn't exist
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Reviewer flagged zero logging but did not specifically call out misleading
    SECURITY comments claiming logging exists when it doesn't.
- finding_id: I6
  title: Non-ASCII tenant header silently treated as missing
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No test was written for non-ASCII tenant header values. TEA tests cover
    auth headers but not X-Tenant-ID with non-ASCII characters.
- finding_id: I7
  title: "CWE-209 test gap \u2014 no body assertion"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: TEA wrote CWE-209 tests in security.rs but reviewer verified 'CWE-209
    properly addressed' without noting the body assertion gap. The test checks status
    code but not response body content.
- finding_id: I8
  title: CORS preflight test doesn't verify CORS headers
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No CORS preflight test exists in the test files. CORS was not part of
    the TEA test plan and the reviewer did not flag CORS header verification gaps.
- finding_id: I9
  title: "Wrong log levels \u2014 error! for 4xx client errors"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Reviewer flagged zero logging (I4) but since no logging was added by Dev,
    the wrong-log-level issue never manifested. No phase addressed log level differentiation
    between 4xx and 5xx.
- finding_id: I10
  title: CORS allows Any origin/method/header (CWE-942)
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No CORS middleware was mentioned in the code changes summary. No test
    covers CORS origin/method/header restrictions. Reviewer did not flag CWE-942.
